LOCATION 
The  Institute  is  located  30  kilometers  from  Kilifi  town 
along   Vitengeni   road. Godoma   TTI   is   adjacent   to 
Arabuko Sokoke Forest and next to Vitengeni Baptist 
Secondary School in Matanomanne market in Ganze 
Sub-county. 
MOTTO 
Quality   learning   for   academic   and   technological 
excellence. 
VISION 
A center of excellence in technological training. 
MISSION 
To become a world class TVET institution in training for 
economic development. 
FACILITY 
The institute stands on 26 acres of land and has two 
storey buildings. Two electrical    engineering 
workshops,  four  building  technology  labs,  four  fully 
equipped  building  technology  workshops,  a  lecture 
theater,   land   scaped   facility   and   state-of-the-art 
equipment and offices adorn the institute. 
ACCOMODATION 
The institute leased modern hostels to accommodate 
trainees who wish to be boarders at an affordable cost 
which provide adequate accommodation for both male 
and female trainees of “first come first serve basis”. 
AFFIRMATIVE ACTION 
Godoma Technical Training Institute encourage female 
trainees to undertake Science, Engineering and Technical 
(SET) courses. 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
Extra-Curricular Activities - High Jump 
 
EXTRA CURRICULAR ACTIVITIES 
We offer a wide range of extra-curricular activities such 
as Sports and Games, Drama, Music and actively 
participate in TVET fairs and shows. 
REVISED FEE & ADMISSION CONDITIONS 
Tuition fees have been reduced from KSh 35,000 to 
KSh 22,396 to make education more affordable for all. 
To ensure inclusivity, the following flexible payment 
options apply: 
1. Self-Sponsored Applicants 
(Those not applying for government support) 
 Pay 50% of the total fee before joining 
 Applies to all courses, including short courses 
2. Government-Supported Applicants 
(Higher Education Loans Board, Kenya Universities and 
Colleges Central Placement Service, bursaries) 
 Pay KSh 5,000 commitment fee 
 Provide proof of application 
3. Sponsored Applicants 
(NGOs, well-wishers, etc.) 
 Pay KSh 2,000 commitment fee 
 Provide a sponsor commitment letters
 
 
 
